<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd">

    <!--
      350 — backing_service_mode: rename the object-storage service id
      'object-store' -> 'velero-objectstore' (hugmesh-admin-bff-api#58, operator decision 92 = A).

      WHY: BackingServiceCatalog called this service 'object-store' while the generator's
      registry (specs/cluster/backing-services.yaml) and the image builder's accepted list
      (build-rpi5-stage4.sh _MGD_TIER12_IDS) call it 'velero-objectstore'. A recorded intent for
      'object-store' named an id the builder dies on ("unknown backing-service id"). The catalog
      now carries 'velero-objectstore'; a row still saying 'object-store' would name an id the
      catalog no longer knows, so its current mode would be orphaned.

      WHETHER ANY ROW EXISTS IS UNKNOWN. Nobody has read a live database. It is unlikely — the
      feature ships dark (app.backing-services.enabled defaults false, and the endpoint refuses
      while dark) — so this changeSet is written to be a no-op on the expected empty case and
      correct on the unexpected one.

      IDEMPOTENT: a plain UPDATE ... WHERE service_id = 'object-store'. Re-executed (or run on a
      database that never had such a row) it matches zero rows and changes nothing. Portable
      (no dbms precondition), so it runs on the H2 test harness as well as Postgres.

      THE APPEND-ONLY LEDGER. backing_service_mode rows are never UPDATEd by the application (the
      adminbff_app GRANT stays SELECT, INSERT — 310). This is a one-time VOCABULARY correction run
      by Liquibase under the migration (owner) role, not an app-side edit: each row keeps its id,
      mode, endpoint, creds_ref, actor, created_at and generation; only the spelling of the same
      service's id changes. The unique index (service_id, generation) cannot collide: no
      'velero-objectstore' row can pre-date this changeSet, because the catalog refused that id
      until the same release that ships this file.

      NOT rewritten: notification_outbox payloads ({"service_id":"object-store",...}) already
      emitted for such a row. Those are delivered notification history, not state anything
      reads back as an id.

      Band 350: the next free band above the current max wired band (340 domain-theme).
      Appended LAST at the include site.
    -->

    <changeSet id="350-backing-service-id-velero-objectstore" author="hugmesh">
        <comment>hugmesh-admin-bff-api#58 / decision 92: rewrite any backing_service_mode row whose
                 service_id is the retired 'object-store' to the registry id 'velero-objectstore'.
                 Idempotent (matches zero rows on re-run or on an empty ledger).</comment>
        <update tableName="backing_service_mode">
            <column name="service_id" value="velero-objectstore"/>
            <where>service_id = 'object-store'</where>
        </update>
        <rollback>
            <update tableName="backing_service_mode">
                <column name="service_id" value="object-store"/>
                <where>service_id = 'velero-objectstore'</where>
            </update>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
